u9m = u6x + RUSH_STAGE 24 (new switch; structural, plateau step 6: the opening rush's shape, not its dose). An opening
rusher (born by RUSH_LAST r17) heading for its rush target (the nearest live mirror spot; no enemy king seen) holds,
facing the target, once it is inside the stage line: within Chebyshev 24 of the target but farther than 6, and 3+ from
its king's spawn tile. It leaves at the launch round, when the last opening rusher can have walked from home to the
line: r17 + 5/4 of (Chebyshev home-target - 24) + 4 slack (DefaultMedium's 36: r36). So the rushers that walked out one
a round leave the line together and reach the enemy king as a group. Replacement rushers born later go as in u6x.
COMBAT.md §8: "mass arrival beats per-turn kill caps": a defence that stops one rat a turn cannot stop many at once.
Evidence:
  - rush.py over the 522 u6x-era replica games: the rush killed a king by r200 in 41 (8%), and every such game was won.
    Against Varun, in the 17 kills 7.7 rushers reached Chebyshev 4 of its king (the first at r18, the 4th at r32) and
    3.8 died on the way; in the 163 others 2.8 arrived (the first at r44.5) and 7.2 died on the way (thrown 2.0,
    trapped 1.9, cats 2.0). Xzibit: 5.6 arrived in kills, 1.8 otherwise; Merlin 11.0 against 1.4. Rushers born r4-17
    walk out one a round and meet the enemy's half alone.
  - Where they die: rushers dead before arriving fall a median 13-19 tiles from the enemy king (0.5-0.68 of the way
    from ours), so the line sits at 24, before that band; a rally next to the king would form inside it.
  - Flippable cells (635 u6x-era matches, 69 mixed cells): our king-kill wins come at a median r78 against Varun, r44
    against Icarus and r60 against Merlin, so in those cells the opening rush decides the game.
  - The twin's sets (rush.py ALL): set 3 (13248-13291) arrived by r100 2.12 a game, rush kills 3 of 48, dead before
    arriving 5.31; set 1 (12771-12813) 2.48, 4, 5.79; set 2 (12838-12899) 1.58, 5, 6.33.
  - Two earlier forms failed in a local game (DefaultMedium vs u6x) before any screen: a rally 5 from our king until
    r24 strung out on the way (at r44 three rushers led the other nine by 7 tiles), and a walk-on-even-rounds head
    rule never fired (side-by-side rushers each counted the other as ahead and leapfrogged; distances matched u6x's
    through r36). This form, same game: 9 rushers held at Chebyshev 18-22 of u6x's king through r36 and were still
    within 10-18 of it at r45 (6 within 10-12); 0 overruns; points win 52-47, no king died before r458. On that map
    the nearest mirror spot (VERTICAL, 20 from home) is inside the line, so the rushers first held 3 from home until
    r21, then retargeted to the true king and held on its line.
  - RUSH_TO, RUSH_DIST, RUSH_LIFE, RUSH_BURN and RUSH_UNTIL 200/500 (doses of the stream) were each rejected on the
    replica, and u8z (no rush) failed its screen: the rush pays for itself, but arrives piecemeal.
